Description: relay a Reachy Mini camera, mic and speakers as Linux virtual devices
 reachy-mini-cam-relay connects to a Reachy Mini over WebRTC and exposes its
 camera, microphone and speakers as Linux virtual devices (v4l2loopback plus
 PulseAudio/PipeWire sinks), so any browser meeting app (Jitsi, Meet, Teams,
 Discord, ...) can use them for full two-way telepresence.
 .
 The Python application and all of its Python dependencies are bundled in a
 self-contained virtualenv under /opt/venvs; only the system media libraries
 (GStreamer, v4l2loopback, PulseAudio) are shared with the host.
